# AGP 9.3 composes this directory with optimized Android defaults and the
# consumer rules embedded in releaseRuntimeClasspath. See docs/R8.md for sources.
#
# AndroidX / Compose / Navigation: use their consumer rules and generated
# manifest/resource entry points. No blanket keep for Activities or ViewModels.
# kotlinx.serialization: bundled rules retain generated serializers for DTOs
# and typed navigation routes. There are no serializable named companions.
# Ktor / coroutines: bundled rules cover atomic fields and engine/dispatcher
# discovery. HttpClient also selects the OkHttp engine explicitly.
# OkHttp: bundled Android rules cover optional TLS providers.
# MapLibre: its AAR retains JNI entry points, GeoJSON and Gson JSON tree classes;
# AndroidX @Keep rules cover its annotated native callbacks.
# Koin / Orbit: app factories and containers use direct references, without
# reflective constructor lookup. No extra keep rules are needed for this usage.
# Timber: release logging is disabled in code; use its bundled consumer rules.
#
# No additional app-specific keep or dontwarn rules are currently required.
# Add only narrowly scoped rules for demonstrated reflection/JNI entry points.
# Never hide missing classes globally or keep entire dependency/app packages.
